      <div class="reveal"><h2>I think in <em>mechanisms</em> — whether the reactor is stainless steel or a cell wall.</h2><p>I'm drawn to the seams between disciplines: the point where a materials trade-off in a design course turns out to matter just as much for a water filter serving a real community as it does on paper. <em>I don't pick a side between the engineering and the people it's for</em> — I want to understand both well enough to move between them without losing precision.</p><p>That habit started before McMaster — four years leading a DECA chapter back from the edge of closure, sitting on my district's Student Senate, and mentoring incoming students through Link Crew taught me how to turn a plan into something that actually works for people. I bring the same instinct to engineering now: I care about getting the numbers right, so I back every design with data, trade-off analysis, and a method someone else could rerun.</p><p class="personal-note">The short version: I like technical work, I like people, and I'm happiest when a project lets me care about both.</p>
        <ul class="now"><li>Researching UV water purification and co-authoring public science articles with The Student Water Project</li><li>Training with the braking sub-team for McMaster's AIChE Chem-E-Car competition</li><li>Finishing Level 2 of my B.Eng. in Chemical Engineering & Bioengineering at McMaster</li></ul>
        <div class="tools"><div><strong>Laboratory techniques</strong><ul class="chips"><li>Acid-base titration</li><li>UV-Vis spectrophotometry</li><li>Gravimetric / vacuum filtration</li><li>Calorimetry</li><li>Galvanic cell assembly</li></ul></div><div><strong>Software & programming</strong><ul class="chips"><li>SolidWorks</li><li>GRANTA</li><li>Python</li><li>MATLAB</li><li>Java</li><li>Excel</li></ul></div><div><strong>Certifications & safety</strong><ul class="chips"><li>WHMIS</li><li>Health & Safety</li><li>SAFE</li><li>Chemical Handling & Spills</li><li>Gas Cylinder Safety</li></ul></div><div><strong>Coursework</strong><ul class="chips"><li>Project Design (1P13)</li><li>Materials & Manufacturing</li><li>Chemical Process Principles</li><li>Bioengineering Foundations</li></ul></div></div>
